   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Action.lean:86-87 defines `objEquiv` with `toFun x := x`, and `coe_back` (line 77) is the lemma for `back \u2191x = x`. The PR's proof ends `rw [ActionCategory.stabilizerMulEquivAut_apply_hom_hom]; exact Iff.rfl` with goal `\u2191g \u2208 germKernel G (objEquiv G X x).back \u2194 \u2191g \u2208 germKernel G x`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/CategoryTheory/ActionGroupoid/Effective.lean",
   "fix": "Make the last step explicit by rewriting with `ActionCategory.coe_back`, or add a `@[simp]` lemma `(objEquiv G X x).back = x`. Then replace the rewrite chain and `Iff.rfl` with `simp [..., toEffective_map_eq_id_iff]`.",
   "issue": "`Effective.ker_stabilizerToAut` rewrites through seven named lemmas (`MonoidHom.mem_ker, Subgroup.mem_subgroupOf, Aut.ext_iff, Aut.one_asIso, Iso.ext_iff, Iso.refl_hom, stabilizerToAut_apply_asIso_hom`) and then ends with `exact Iff.rfl`, which only works because `(ActionCategory.objEquiv G X x).back` unfolds to `x`. No comment explains this, and the chain will break on Mathlib renames.",
   "line": 271
  }
